course: dictionary
lesson: 2941
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word dress can be a thing you wear, or an action, such as putting clothes on. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00.» The clues are breakfast, washing and get up. They are all part of the morning routine, so dressing means putting clothes on.
explain: «Picture a wedding in a hotel near Galway: your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress.» Here dress is a thing you wear. The clues are bridesmaid and wedding, so dress is a noun, a piece of clothing.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «dressing» means putting clothes on, the sentence still makes sense. If it doesn't, try another meaning.
fact: Dress can be a noun (a dress, dresses) or a verb (dress, dressed, dressing).
fact: «Dress» as a noun means a piece of clothing that covers the body from the shoulders down to the legs, in one piece.
fact: «Dressed» as a verb means putting clothes on yourself or someone else, as in «get dressed».
fact: «Dress» can also mean cleaning a wound and covering it with a bandage, or adding sauce to food, as in «dress a salad».
fact: Phrases: «fancy dress» (UK) and «costume party» (USA) mean dressing up as characters, as on World Book Day or Halloween.
exercise: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00.» What does dressing mean here? | *Putting clothes on yourself | Cleaning a cut | Cooking a salad | Singing loudly
exercise: «Your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress.» What is a dress here? | A sauce for a salad | A kind of hat | *A piece of clothing in one piece, from the shoulders to the legs | A way to clean a wound
exercise: «Toad, still dressed as a washerwoman, tells her a sad made-up story.» What does dressed as a washerwoman mean? | Singing a sad song | *Wearing clothes that make him look like a washerwoman | Cooking a meal for the family | Washing clothes in the river
test: «When Odysseus got home, he came in dressed as a beggar.» What does this tell us? | Odysseus had no home and no money | Odysseus gave away all his food | *Odysseus wore clothes to look like a beggar, so nobody knew who he was | Odysseus was feasting in the hall
test: «The nurse will dress the cut on your knee.» What does dress mean here? | To add sauce to food | To put on a costume | To brush your hair | *To clean the cut and cover it with a bandage
exam: «Dress for the weather» means which of these? | Hide in the dark | Add a sauce to your food | Clean a cut and cover it | *Choose clothes that keep you warm, dry or cool
